	pages = {092501},
	annote = {Lit review §2.4What: ZnSO4 flow through a Cu mesh anode; 2D COMSOL (laminar flow + dilute species + secondary current distribution).
Numbers: 0.01–1 M ZnSO4; 0.5 mm/s flow: Zn–Cu life 18 → 1300 cycles @50 mA/cm²; benefit at Pe {\textgreater} 1 (abstract).
Relevance: medium — one of few COMSOL Zn sulfate models tied to experiment. INT. Abstract only.11 Nov: full text read. BCs stated explicitly: normal inflow velocity, zero-pressure outlet, symmetry sides, no-slip and uniform potential on a 30 µm wire (Fig. 7a) — counter-example to the undocumented separator FEM (B1). Relevance raised to high.},
