	annote = {Lit review §2.4What: sulfonated cellulose acetate nanofibre membrane on Zn; COMSOL with the fibres resolved as circles and ellipses of different sizes/angles, sparse (porous) vs dense coating (Fig. 4f,g, Fig. S18–S19; simulation sections read via Europe PMC).
Numbers: Zn with three protrusions (Fig. S18); outputs E-field and c(Zn²⁺); "consistent with" chronoamperometry at −150 mV (Fig. 4h) — qualitative only; interface, BCs, parameters n/r in main text.
Relevance: high — the only Zn paper found that resolves fibre cross-sections like the group's hollow-circle NDs; Shanghai → CN.},
